From 52535e8000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: GameSpark <gamespark@localhost>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 23:30:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] x86 hardware execute breakpoints (DR0-DR3/DR7) for Wine guests

Local GameSpark patch, not submitted upstream (FEX does not accept AI-generated code). Enabled with FEX_GSHWBP=1;
needs FEX_NEEDSSECCOMP=1 too (it disables inline syscalls, so every syscall returns through the hook).

Denuvo arms an execute breakpoint on its own thread with NtSetContextThread (DR3, DR7=0x40) and expects
EXCEPTION_SINGLE_STEP when the address runs. wineserver sets debug registers with ptrace(PTRACE_POKEUSER) at
offsetof(struct user, u_debugreg[i]); FEX answered EPERM. Now:
- ptrace PEEKUSER/POKEUSER of the debug registers go through a per-thread shared-memory mailbox
  (/dev/shm/fexhwbp-<tid>) that each guest thread creates and applies at its next syscall return;
- armed addresses are reference counted process-wide; the frontend makes an armed address the entry of its own
  compile unit, and the JIT emits a check there against the current thread's DR0-3/DR7 that raises a guest #DB
  (SIGTRAP, trapno 1, TRAP_HWBKPT, DR6 bit set) with RIP at the breakpoint.
Data breakpoints are not implemented (logged). Mailboxes of dead threads are removed at the next process start.
The debug registers are per-thread state in CpuStateFrame, outside CPUState, so signal frames do not restore them
and clone does not copy them (like Linux and Windows); a thread's armed addresses are released when it exits. The
entry check compares without touching NZCV (the guest's flags at block entry); arming flushes the thread's
call-return stack so a pending return cannot skip the check; TF single-steps set DR6.BS; HWBPLock is taken with
signals masked; the mailbox page is reserved with posix_fallocate so a full /dev/shm fails at creation.
